# Forge developer guide

Keep business features in `src/{{ model.names.namespace }}/Domains/<Feature>/`. Platform tenancy code is grouped under `Platform/Tenancy/`; metadata endpoints are under `Platform/Meta/`. Infrastructure supplies authentication, validation, database access and the HTTP pipeline. V1 contract and persisted entity namespaces remain stable; other internal host imports transition to .Platform. Program.cs is the minimal entry point.

Start with [DeveloperReference/Portability.md](DeveloperReference/Portability.md) for automatic module registration, feature structure, business routes, contracts and upgrades. A service layer is optional: simple CRUD may inject the tenant repository directly. Each request DTO has its own file.

- [Database](DeveloperReference/Database.md): connection settings, secrets, health checks and migration commands.
- [Tenancy quick start](DeveloperReference/TenancyQuickStart.md): tenant entities, configurations, repository access and isolation tests.
- [Tenancy](DeveloperReference/Tenancy.md): platform tenant management and background scopes.
- [Authentication](DeveloperReference/Authentication.md): authentication and authorization configuration.
- [Trusted provisioning](DeveloperReference/TrustedProvisioning.md): administrative user lifecycle.
Optional sanitization and OData references are emitted when those modules are selected.

Run `dotnet build` and `dotnet test` before review. Run architecture and migration drift checks after moving code. Copy feature tests with their feature when upgrading, and retain the fresh print's platform tests.

For an existing database preserve its complete migration lineage and snapshot before appending any new migrations. Never baseline over existing tables. Review [the upgrade procedure](DeveloperReference/Portability.md) before replacing a print.


## Observability

Every service method must be instrumented. Ship no dark code. See [DeveloperReference/Observability.md](DeveloperReference/Observability.md) for what the service already emits, the settings each environment needs, and how to triage a production issue.

### Logging

```csharp
// Normal operations
_logger.LogInformation("Fetching record {RecordId}", id);

// Expected failures
_logger.LogWarning("Record {RecordId} not found", id);

// Unexpected failures
_logger.LogError(ex, "Failed to create record with reference {Reference}", request.Reference);
```

**Rules:** Never log PII. Always use structured properties � never string interpolation in log messages.

### Tracing

Use `ForgeTelemetry.ActivitySource`. It is registered with OpenTelemetry, so spans are exported. Do not create your own `ActivitySource`: its spans would be silently dropped.

```csharp
using var activity = ForgeTelemetry.ActivitySource.StartActivity("{{ model.manifest.service_name }}.get");
activity?.SetTag("record.id", id);
```

An exception that escapes a request is recorded on the request's span automatically. Leave the span status alone.

### Metrics

Use `ForgeTelemetry.Meter`. It is registered with OpenTelemetry, so its instruments are exported. Do not create your own `Meter`.

```csharp
private static readonly Counter<long> OperationsCounter =
    ForgeTelemetry.Meter.CreateCounter<long>("{{ model.manifest.service_name }}.operations", "{operation}", "Domain operations.");

OperationsCounter.Add(1, new TagList { { "operation", "get" }, { "result", "success" } });
```

---

## Switching OIDC provider

Pervaxis supports any OIDC-compliant identity provider. Change `Forge:Oidc:Provider` and set `Authority` + `Audience` accordingly. No code changes required � configuration only.

**Cognito** is handled by the platform as well, with its own checks (access tokens only, allowed app clients, admin group). For Cognito set `ClientIds` instead of `Audience`. Settings, policies and examples are in [`DeveloperReference/Authentication.md`](DeveloperReference/Authentication.md).

| Provider | Authority URL | Audience |
|---|---|---|
| Auth0 | `https://{domain}/` | `https://your-api` |
| Supabase | `https://{project}.supabase.co/auth/v1` | `authenticated` |
| Okta | `https://{domain}/oauth2/default` | `api://default` |
| Cognito | `https://cognito-idp.{region}.amazonaws.com/{pool-id}` | not used. Set `ClientIds` to the app client IDs |

Example (`appsettings.json`):

```json
{
  "Forge": {
    "Oidc": {
      "Provider": "Okta",
      "Authority": "https://dev-123456.okta.com/oauth2/default",
      "Audience": "api://default",
      "Domain": ""
    }
  }
}
```

The `Domain` property is retained for Auth0 management API compatibility and can be left empty for other providers.

---


Ownership: Platform contains print-owned runtime code; Domains contains business modules. Data/Migrations is application-owned upgrade history and snapshot state, excluded from Platform replacement. See [the ownership and upgrade policy](DeveloperReference/Ownership.md).
